{"type":"npc","name":"Synthecite Vivisectionist","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":115,"temp":0,"max":115,"details":""},"ac":{"value":25,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":35,"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"climb","value":10}],"details":""},"immunities":[{"type":"disease","exceptions":[]},{"type":"poison","exceptions":[]}],"weaknesses":[{"type":"precision","value":10,"exceptions":[]}],"resistances":[{"type":"bleed","value":10,"exceptions":[],"doubleVs":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["common","diabolic","shadowtongue","venenan"],"details":""},"level":{"value":7},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Synthecite vivisectionists are a variety of fleshwarps, people whose bodies and minds have been twisted by various magical or alchemical processes. In this case, all synthecites, vivisectionists included, found their forms and intellects completely corrupted and reshaped into something new by a sentient poison called synthecite substrate. This poison is the prized creation of a velstrac demagogue who seeks to \"improve\" mortal life into a new superior form. Those who would perish from the poison are instead agonizingly reborn, becoming new synthecites with a religious devotion to the demagogue. Their doctrine compels them to spread their transformation to all mortals, whether by sneaking the substrate into small village wells, infecting crops to gradually corrupt the masses, or directly injecting mortals and removing their rebellious flesh for more expedient results.</p><p>Synthecite vivisectionists have two main features (besides their horrific appearance of course): a hollow bone spike on one arm that they use to inject a substance into their victims and two bone scythes over their shoulders that they skillfully use to make unwanted surgeries that speed up the transformation process.</p><p>Though the vast majority of people who are exposed to synthecite substrate turn into new synthecite vivisectionists, the bodies of particularly skilled individuals occasionally react differently, morphing into a stronger variety of synthecite that retains some of the abilities the person originally held in life, if not their morals, priorities, or outlook. Examples of some of these synthecite variants include stealthy horripolators, adaptable eugenicists, and zealous flense-priests.</p><h2>Half of the Time, It Works Every Time</h2><p>Synthecite vivisectionist doctrine holds that synthecite substrate never fails, inevitably transforming its subjects into new vivisectionists. On occasion, though, a would-be victim shakes off the poison, either through robust health or curative magic. When this happens, vivisectionists see the survivor as a personal insult and a threat to the natural order, targeting the heretical survivor for instant destruction.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 45/100/180 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (bludgeoning, piercing, slashing), armor (medium), perception item, skill items (Athletics, Intimidation, Lore [Synthecite], Medicine)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> body, bane, constitution, energy resistant (vitality), poison, poisonous armor, sensory (darkvision, greater darkvision), spiked, strength, unholy, wild</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"Jameson Knopp","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":6},"dex":{"mod":2},"con":{"mod":4},"int":{"mod":2},"wis":{"mod":2},"cha":{"mod":3}},"perception":{"details":"painsight","mod":13,"senses":[{"type":"greater-darkvision"}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":17,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":15,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":13,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"athletics":{"base":17},"intimidation":{"base":16},"medicine":{"base